JDK 17 case mapping, character properties and word-boundary data

Generated using the open-source Eclipse Temurin runtime identified in SOURCES.json.
data.inc and character.inc retain GPLv2 with the Classpath exception; LICENSE contains those terms.
Unicode and ICU notices are preserved separately. The factual case mappings,
character properties and OpenJDK ROOT word-break automata are used by src/case.inc.
The original OpenJDK RuleBasedBreakIterator, ConditionalSpecialCasing and
BreakIteratorRules sources are preserved without changes, with their notices.
The adapted C boundary traversal in src/case.inc uses the same GPLv2 + Classpath
exception. Other project files retain their stated licenses.
GenerateCaseData.java is original project code under the root MIT license.
GenerateCharacterData.java is also original MIT project code. character.inc
contains Unicode 13 character classifications and radix-digit values generated
from the same pinned Temurin runtime; it is consumed by src/character.inc.
The Temurin executable is a local build dependency and is not redistributed.
